!node Bugs

Currently, there is no bug known. 

Please sends your bug report to the Authors.

!node Historic

!begin_description
 !item [2.33] Minor release. 
	!begin_itemize
	!item added new function ldg_callback() that save/restore A2/D2 registers
	!item enhanced loading of ldg: now a directory may be part of the filename
	      (for example "windom/userdef.ldg" or "zcodec/jpeg.ldg").
	!end_itemize

 !item [2.32] Minor release. 
	!begin_itemize
	!item LDG is now distributed under conditions specified by the LESSER
	GNU PUBLIC LICENCE (see file COPYRIGHT in this distribution for
	details about this licence).
	!end_itemize

 !item [2.31] Minor release. 
	!begin_itemize
	!item one bug has been fixed on the way LDG looks for a library when 
          one specify its path with MiNT convention.
        !item the developper C library is now totaly independant on
          the GEM library used. Note for developper : as  LDG is independant of 
          the GEM library, you need to specify the GEM header file before 
          including 'ldg.h'.
        !item LDG and its utilities have been recompiled used the last version of 
          Gemlib (pl43).
        !item Using ldg devel library, it is not necessary to link a GEM library
          if your LDG does not require it.
	!end_itemize
!item [2.30] Major release. Important bugs had been fixed :
!begin_itemize
!item  Scratch register problem fixed (Arnaud Bercegeay).
!item  Problems with MiNT fixed.
!item  New function ldg_cpush() to deal with 68040 - 68060 cache.
!item  New version of ldginfo.ttp (formely showlib.ttp).
!item  New LDG code error LDG_NOFUNC.
!item  Library developpement version number and TSR version
	   number are aligned to 2.30.
!item  When it is possible (MiNT and MagiC), libraries are loaded
       in shared memory (dev/shm). LDG kernel offers a way to
	   share user memory. MEM.LDG uses it to share memory.
	   For that, LDG deamon is required running. This is totally transparency 
	   for the user (or developper).
!item  Great thanx to Arnaud for its help and contributions !
!end_itemize
   
!item [2.11] Minor release. The GEM installer works with long 
	filename system, the default configuration of TSR (LDG.PRG) 
	can be changed (using SHOWLIB.TTP). So you can use LDG without 
	the LDG CPX. 

!item [2.10]
!begin_itemize
!item  correction of a small which occurs when a client loads several 
  times a same library,
!item  new version of CPX and SHOWLIB (a LDG tool). These updates are
  due to the previous bug correction,
!item  new version (2.00) of LDGMGR.APP. This application is the LDG 
  manager used by client compiled with LDG 1.xx. It is supplied for 
  backward compatibility. This version provides a better compatibility
  between LDG 1 and 2.
!item  last release of LDG INFO (written by A.Bercegeay), a very usefull tool
  for LDG-libraries managing.
!end_itemize

!item [2.00] This version is  a major evolution  of LDG :  LDG manager is  now
	 obsolet and, then, the LDG protocol communication between  client
	 and manager - based on AES message - is unused.
     TSR version is 2.20.

!hline 

!item [1.20]  Many  bugs   fixed,  specially  concerning   MiNT  with   memory
     protection. Developper libraries: new function ldg_libexec_evnt()
     TSR : new  functions libexec_event()  and error().  Documentation
     switches to english !
	 TSR version is 2.10.

!item [1.10] TSR : LDG.PRG contains now the functions to load/unload  LDG-lib.
     Thus, languages not  supported by  the LDG  distribution can  now
     handled (as client) the LDG protocol.  A LDG-lib can now call  an
     another LDG-lib (see ldg_libexec()).
     TSR version is 2.00

!item [1.00] The  first  non-beta  version.  (See  the  0.99C   version)
     Showlib.ttp :  version  1.30  Showlip.app  is  removed  from  the
     distribution. Adding Sozobon C support
	 TSR version is 1.00. (TSR does not contain any functions, it is
     just used to configure LDG variables).

!end_description

!hline
Warning : versions older than 1.00 are beta and not public release.
!begin_description
!item [0.99 Release A] New protocol featuring a LDG-manager.
     Different acces of a LDG-lib (resident, locked, unshareable).
!item [0.99 Release B]
     Bug in LDG-manager fixed.
     Showlib version 1.11.
!item [0.99 Release C]
     Dirty bug fixed in the loading LDG function
     Showlib.ttp version 1.00 (a TTP version of Showlib)
     Bug in ldg_cookie() fixed
     LDG-lib can now used a closure function
     LDG_LIST provides now the version of the LDG-manager

!item [0.90] With SingleTOS, LDG works correctly.

!item [0.80] MT_AES library (for using AES from a LDG-LIB)
     Source is compatible GemLib pl 36 and Pure C
     GemLib

!item [0.70] LDG_REQUEST message have changed, the LDG_ANSWER
     message is obsolet

!item [0.60] Gcc 32bits is now supported

!item [0.50] New data structure, some fixed bugs

!item [0.40] GEM messages of the protocol have a new number

!item [0.30] SingleTOS is supported (using a new protocol)

!item [0.20] Extension of the LDG-protocol

!item [0.10] The first version (from Olivier Landemarre)     

!end_description

